# Palomar Comparator safety

- Read `docs/PALOMAR_STYLE.md` before changing compared declarations.
- Read `docs/PALOMAR_EDITORIAL_AUDIT.md` before submission packaging changes.
- Pin universe parameter names and make unstable instance paths explicit.
- Keep every `definition_names` value and every transitively locked
  Challenge/Solution definition structurally identical.
- Audit named child definitions referenced by matching parent bodies; Palomar
  compares those values independently.
- Never use inline proofs in locked structure values: generated
  `._proof_N` constants are mechanically compared.
- Move proof fields to named theorems and list them in `theorem_names`.
- Every material symbol in a compared theorem type must be pinned: either
  defined without `sorry` in Challenge.lean or listed in `definition_names`.
- Keep `formalization.yaml` aligned with `comparator.json` (`main_results`,
  scope, limitations, sources).
- Challenge may contain proof holes; Solution and `Scott1964/**/*.lean` may not.
- **CI / routine edits:** `bash scripts/palomar_preflight.sh --mechanical-only`
  (includes Palomar-pinned `../palomar-preflight/verify-comparator.sh`)
- **Before Palomar submission:** full `bash scripts/palomar_preflight.sh`
  (mechanical + editorial LLM audit). Do not claim readiness unless mechanical
  preflight passes; treat editorial `neutral` synthesis as the submission bar.
